/-!
# The Clifford group `C_n`

Corresponds to LaTeX section `Clifford.tex`.

`C_n` is defined in `df:Clifford` as the normalizer of `P_n` inside `U_n`,
i.e. those unitaries `c` such that conjugation by `c` sends `P_n` to itself.

Following the paper we want to:

* define `Clifford n` as a subgroup of `Unitary n`,
* produce three families of generators `H_i`, `P_i`, `CNOT_{i,j}`
  (`lem:HinC`, `lem:PinC`, `lem:CNOTinC`),
* state that those generate the whole group (`thm:Clifford`),
* define the "Clifford mapping" `M[c] : PauliOp n → PauliOp n`
  (`df:CliffordMap`).
-/

namespace GottesmanKnill

/-- The image of `PauliOp.toUnitary`: the unitaries that come from a Pauli.
This is the formal version of `P_n ⊆ U_n` used in the definition of the
normalizer. -/
noncomputable def pauliImage (n : ℕ) : Subgroup (Unitary n) :=
  (PauliOp.toUnitary (n := n)).range

/-- The Clifford group `C_n`.

In the paper: `C_n = N(P_n) ∩ U_n`. Since we already have a `Subgroup` of
`Unitary n`, we just take its normalizer.

(`Subgroup.normalizer` in Mathlib is the set of `g` such that `g H g⁻¹ = H`,
matching `df:Normalizer` and `df:Clifford` exactly.) -/
noncomputable def Clifford (n : ℕ) : Subgroup (Unitary n) :=
  Subgroup.normalizer (pauliImage n)

