/-! ### Generators: `H_i`, `P_i`, `CNOT_{i,j}` are Clifford

The three lemmas `lem:HinC`, `lem:PinC`, `lem:CNOTinC` in the paper depend on
the matrix identities `eq:Basischange`, `eq:phaseconj`, `eq:cnotconj`. In our
abstract setup we *introduce* these gates as opaque unitaries with the
required conjugation behavior. -/

/-- The Hadamard gate on qubit `i`. -/
axiom H {n : ℕ} (i : Fin n) : Unitary n

/-- The phase (`S`) gate on qubit `i`. -/
axiom S {n : ℕ} (i : Fin n) : Unitary n

/-- The CNOT gate with control `i`, target `j`. We require `i ≠ j` —
**TODO(you).** decide whether to bake that into the type. -/
axiom CNOT {n : ℕ} (i j : Fin n) : Unitary n

/-- `lem:HinC`. -/
axiom H_mem_clifford (i : Fin n) : H i ∈ Clifford n

/-- `lem:PinC`. -/
axiom S_mem_clifford (i : Fin n) : S i ∈ Clifford n

/-- `lem:CNOTinC`. -/
axiom CNOT_mem_clifford (i j : Fin n) : CNOT i j ∈ Clifford n

/-- The "generator set" of `C_n`: `{H_i, P_i, CNOT_{i,j}}`. -/
def generators (n : ℕ) : Set (Unitary n) :=
  {u : Unitary n | (∃ i : Fin n, u = H i) ∨ (∃ i : Fin n, u = S i) ∨ (∃ i j : Fin n, u = CNOT i j)}

/-- `thm:Clifford`: the Clifford group is generated by `H`, `S`, `CNOT`.

In Mathlib language: `Clifford n = Subgroup.closure (generators n)`.
This direction `⊆` is the deep one (every Clifford element is a product of
generators); the converse `⊇` follows from the three `_mem_clifford` axioms above. -/
